From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:32:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/60] MAS local: never upload usage metrics

Not for upstream: it is the opposite of the upstream design.

With -metrics-collection, MetricsReporter::start() created a
PlaystoreMetricsWriter. It queues every usage event of the session and,
when the writer is destroyed at exit, gzips them into a LogRequest
(installation id, OS name and version, emulator version, the events) and
posts it to https://play.googleapis.com/log with libcurl.

This build never sends usage metrics, so -metrics-collection no longer
creates any writer: it behaves like -no-metrics and logs one line saying
that the metrics are not uploaded. Nothing else creates a
PlaystoreMetricsWriter. -metrics-to-console and -metrics-to-file still
write the metrics locally, and the Android Studio opt-in still only
writes spool files.

Crash reports are covered by "MAS local: never upload crash reports"
(-metrics-collection also counted as crash upload consent there).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: I2b439198e9e9696d423d7af6d050484afdb99afa
---
 .../metrics/src/android/metrics/MetricsReporter.cpp   | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/emu/metrics/src/android/metrics/MetricsReporter.cpp b/android/emu/metrics/src/android/metrics/MetricsReporter.cpp
index f23fbd383..0eace2ced 100644
--- a/android/emu/metrics/src/android/metrics/MetricsReporter.cpp
+++ b/android/emu/metrics/src/android/metrics/MetricsReporter.cpp
@@ -29,7 +29,6 @@
 #include "android/metrics/MetricsLogging.h"          // for D
 #include "android/metrics/MetricsPaths.h"            // for getSpoolDirectory
 #include "android/metrics/NullMetricsReporter.h"     // for NullMetricsRep...
-#include "android/metrics/PlaystoreMetricsWriter.h"  // for PlaystoreMetri...
 #include "android/metrics/StudioConfig.h"            // for getAnonymizati...
 #include "android/metrics/TextMetricsWriter.h"       // for TextMetricsWriter
 #include "android/utils/debug.h"                     // for dwarning
@@ -103,9 +102,13 @@ void MetricsReporter::start(const std::string& sessionId,
 
     } else if (getConsoleAgents()
             ->settings->android_cmdLineOptions()->metrics_collection) {
-        D("Writing metrics to play store");
-        writer = PlaystoreMetricsWriter::create(sessionId,
-                base::pj(getSpoolDirectory(), "backoff_cookie.proto"));
